# Zepto E-Commerce Sales & Inventory Analysis (SQL)

Data cleaning and business analysis of a Zepto (quick-commerce) product catalog using MySQL — from raw, inconsistent data to category-level revenue and inventory insights.

## Tech Stack
MySQL

## Dataset
A single `zepto` table of product listings with the following columns:

Column                                  Description 
`Category`                            Product category 
`name`                                 Product name 
`mrp`                               Maximum retail price 
`discountPercent`                     Discount applied 
`discountedSellingPrice`      Final selling price after discount 
`availableQuantity`               Units currently in stock 
`outOfStock`                    Stock status (true/false) 
`weightInGms`                        Product weight 
`quantity`                        Order quantity field 

## Data Cleaning
- Checked every column for null values
- Identified and removed records with `mrp = 0` (invalid/placeholder rows)
- Converted `mrp` and `discountedSellingPrice` from paise to rupees (`/ 100`)
- Flagged duplicate product names appearing more than once in the catalog

## Business Questions Answered
1. Top 10 best-value products by discount percentage
2. Products with a high MRP (> ₹300) that are out of stock
3. Estimated revenue per category (`discountedSellingPrice × availableQuantity`)
4. Products priced above ₹500 with less than 10% discount
5. Top 5 categories by average discount percentage
6. Price-per-gram value for products over 100g, ranked best value to worst
7. Products segmented into Low / Medium / Bulk weight tiers
8. Total inventory weight per category

## SQL Skills Demonstrated
- Data cleaning with `DELETE` / `UPDATE` on real-world messy data
- Aggregate functions (`SUM`, `AVG`, `COUNT`) with `GROUP BY`
- Conditional logic with `CASE WHEN`
- Filtering, sorting, and `LIMIT`-based ranking
- Derived/calculated columns (e.g. price per gram)

## Files
- `Zepto_analysis_sql.sql` — full cleaning + analysis script, runnable top to bottom in a MySQL client

## How to Run
1. Load the Zepto product dataset into a MySQL database as a table named `zepto`
2. Run `Zepto_analysis_sql.sql` sequentially in MySQL Workbench or the MySQL CLI

